WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.333
Stable Baselines3.

2
00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:06.200
The sane default for applying RL rather than researching it.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:13.267
Stable Baselines3 gives you reliable, tested implementations of the standard algorithms.

4
00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:20.300
PPO, A2C, DQN, SAC, TD3, behind an API that feels like scikit-learn.

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.400
Why does that matter so much in RL?

6
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.396
Because implementations are easy to get subtly wrong.

7
00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:31.581
A famous blog post lists thirty seven details for PPO alone.

8
00:00:31.581 --> 00:00:37.300
With SB3, when a run fails, suspect your environment and reward, not the plumbing.

9
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.133
The workflow is five steps.

10
00:00:40.433 --> 00:00:41.433
Create a model.

11
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:42.533
Call learn.

12
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:43.533
Save it.

13
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:44.933
Load it anywhere.

14
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:46.200
And evaluate.

15
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.367
A few perks.

16
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:53.033
Swapping algorithms is one word, so honest baselines are nearly free.

17
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:59.100
You also get evaluation, checkpoint callbacks, vectorized environments, and TensorBoard logging.

18
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.709
Its boundary is single-machine training with standard algorithms.

19
00:01:03.709 --> 00:01:05.233
Beyond that, use RLlib.

20
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.900
Here is the whole template.

21
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.267
Build a PPO model, and train it.

22
00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:11.128
Save it.

23
00:01:11.128 --> 00:01:11.900
Train once.

24
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.703
Reload it anywhere, and evaluate over twenty episodes.

25
00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:18.233
To swap the algorithm, change one word.

26
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:23.233
LunarLander is the closest gym environment to your space world.

27
00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:26.700
Thrust, gravity, a landing pad, and fuel penalties.

28
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.398
This script is your permanent template.

29
00:01:29.398 --> 00:01:33.333
Your custom telemetry environment drops into the same few lines.

30
00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:37.400
And keep the saved model: it becomes your first registered version.

31
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.483
Let's recap.

32
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:42.500
SB3 gives you tested standard algorithms.

33
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.533
Construct, learn, save, load, evaluate.

34
00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:49.400
Swapping algorithms is one word, so baselines are cheap.

35
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.067
Beyond one machine, use RLlib.

36
00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.567
Next up: Gymnasium.
